  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohit Kumar Behara vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 25 October, 2024 Author: Parth Prateem Sahu Bench: Parth Prateem Sahu 1/4 2024:CGHC:42396 NAFR HIGH COURT OF CHHATTISGARH AT BILASPUR WPS No. 6884 of 2024 1 - Mohit Kumar Behara S/o Shri Chandan Singh Behara Aged About 42 Years Presently Working On The Post Of Food Safety Officer In The Office Of The Deputy Director, Food And Drug Administration, Bilaspur, District Bilaspur Chhattisgarh, R/o Abhishek Vihar, Phase-Ii Quarter No. 152, Mangla, Bilaspur, District Bilaspur, Chhattisgarh ---- Pet versus 1 - State Of Chhattisgarh Through The Additional Chief Secretary, Department Of Health And Family Welfare, Mantralaya, Mahanadi Bhavan, Atal Nagar, Nava Raipur, District Raipur, Chhattisgarh 2 - Commissioner Food Safety, Food And Drug Administration, Indravati Bhawan, Atal Nagar, Nava Raipur, District Raipur, Chhattisgarh 3 - Controller Food And Drug Administration, Indravati Bhawan, Atal Nagar Nava Raipur, District Raipur, Chhattisgarh 4 - Deputy Secretary Department Of Health And Family Welfare, Government Of Chhattisgarh, Mantralaya, Mahanadi Bhavan, Atal Nagar - 492 002, Nava Raipur, District Raipur, Chhattisgarh 5 - Shri Nitesh Kumar Mishra Food Safety Officer Office Of Controller Of Food Balrampur District , Balrampur ---- Respond Mohit Kumar Behara vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 25 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/178400724/ 1 ____________________________________________________________ For Petitioner : Mr. Dhiraj Kumar Wankhede, Advocate For Respondents/State : Ms. Akanksha Verma Dabhadker, P.L. Hon'ble Shri Justice Parth Prateem Sahu Order On Board 25/10/2024 1.",
    "facts": "Petitioner has filed this petition seeking following relief (s) :- \"10.1 Call for the entire records leading to issuance of the impugned communication and impugned order Annexure P-1 for the kind perusal of this Hon'ble Court. 10.3 Pass appropriate orders, in favour of the petitioner, so far as the cost of the litigation and other miscellaneous expenses are concerned. 10.4 Grant any such other relief in favour of petitioner as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit in the interest of justice.\"",
    "arguments": "If petitioner is to shift at transferred place of posting, studies of her daughter will adversely be affected. He submits that in similar circumstances, Hon'ble Supreme Court in case of Director of School Education, Madras & Ors. Vs. O. Karuppa Thevan & Anr, reported in 1994 Suppl. (2) SCC 666 has observed that children of an employee who are studying should be given due weightage. He next contended that wife of petitioner is carrying pregnancy of about six months, therefore, also, shifting of petitioner at this stage may adversely affect health of his wife. Immediately after receipt of order of transfer, petitioner has already submitted representation before respondents on 18.10.2024, however, no decision has been taken on the same till the date. He also contended that petitioner till date has not been relieved from his present place of posting. 5. Considering the submission of learned counsel for parties, nature of grievance raised in particular considering the fact that daughter of petitioner is student of Class -10 th and also the decision of Mohit Kumar Behara vs State Of Chhattisgarh on 25 October, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/178400724/ 2"
  },
